  "body": "CHECK MAINLINE-035 complete: REVISE source readings and conclusions; all 112 comparable derived fields reproduce under the owner’s conventions. Independent tensor-rotation CLT, Vc, R/rho and predecessor lead calculations pass; 25 input pins verified. Owner script was not used.\n\nCalibrated S-II hemisphere centers read about 0.21–0.22, not 0.22–0.24, with approximately ±0.01 graph uncertainty. Add the omitted eleventh cylinder point near R/rho=121, gamma=0.61. Replace the cylinder eye fit with CR-1457’s analytic curve. CTA8.3’s printed 0.864 differs from its stated loads’ 0.865305; retain both pending resolution. CTA8.1 was out-of-autoclave; nominal versus measured thickness changes its Vc.\n\nThe 0.338273/0.295840 handbook cap/cylinder ratios reproduce, but establish no sandwich-shell transfer law. Additional marine egg-shaped/ellipsoidal physical tests and the owner’s omitted leads invalidate categorical absence claims. Yang’s 12.44 MPa collapse is plastic, not a comparable elastic sphere KDF. Anderson’s retrieved thesis is theoretical. Sim’s uniform-pressure results are FE; three inherited numeric claims remain unreconstructed.\n\nNo compatible elastic sphere/dome datum with recoverable moderate Vc at the lead geometry was established. Required lead gamma and the claimed unprecedented imperfection control remain unvalidated. All sourced values QUESTIONABLE; transfers PROJECTION.\n\nExact fields, graph refinements and qualifications are recorded in 71 rows; sixteen nonblocking NFIs preserve the gaps. Brief names no successor; returning to SLEEPING for the next queued job.",
